---
description: Join independent preservation findings without letting one success hide another defect.
args:
  original: Analysis
  impact: ImpactResult
  component: AffectedComponent
  replay: Replay
returns: Audit
---
1. Select the component obligations from impact and retain their complete required meanings and
   protected rules. ClaimedCoverage is a proposal assertion, not the audit's obligation inventory.
2. Call checkCanon(original, replay, obligations), checkKnowledge(original, replay, obligations)
   and checkAmbiguity(original, replay, obligations). Consume every returned SemanticFinding.
3. Consume replay.claimJudgment.unsupportedIds as explicit claimed-coverage findings. Its coveredIds
   are claims checked against the independent specialists, not authority to skip their obligations.
4. Judge physical obligations using original object identity constraints and replay.props. A new
   appearance must not create unsupported custody, copies or capabilities. Add witnessed findings.
5. Judge action motivation using replay.world and replay.knowledge: the rescuer must have a
   supported destination and signal premise at the action event, even when the rescue succeeds.
6. Judge callback obligations using replay.motifs. A repaired reference must preserve its required
   dramatic relation; merely removing the visibly inconsistent noun can destroy the protected meaning.
7. For each obligation, preserve all distinct violated or unresolved findings. A satisfied knowledge
   path cannot override a physical contradiction or a prohibited resolution of uncertainty.
8. Fill missingObligationIds for any component obligation with no substantive finding. An absent
   check is unreviewed coverage, not a default satisfied value.
9. Call storyEvidence.checkEdits on the replay candidate and checkWitnesses for collected findings
   against the appropriate snapshot. Original policy witnesses cite original; edited-scene witnesses
   cite replay. Never verify a replacement quotation against unmodified text.
10. Return candidateId, findings, missingObligationIds and exact checks. A valid candidate requires
   complete coverage, no violated/unresolved required obligation, and valid source mechanics.
11. When an unresolved premise is explicitly allowed by a preservation rule, satisfaction means
    preserving that uncertainty. It is distinct from uncertainty about whether the rule was checked.
